# ★ THE ONE OF THE THREE THAT IS NOT A BUG IN ANY PROGRAM.
#
# The affected product is a DOCUMENT. Every implementation that followed
# DSP0274 1.4.0 correctly has the defect, and no amount of reviewing, fuzzing
# or sanitizing an implementation finds it, because there is nothing wrong with
# the implementation. What is wrong is the paragraph it was written from.
#
# That is why this pin names two specification pins rather than a commit range.
# Both versions were downloaded and read; docs/transcript.md section 3 quotes
# all five definitions from each, and the phrase "[FINISH].SPDM Header Fields"
# occurs five times in 1.4.0 and zero times in 1.4.1.
#
# ★★ AND THE ENUMERATION WAS NOT WRONG WHEN IT WAS WRITTEN. In SPDM 1.3 a
# FINISH was a four-byte header followed by its authenticator, so "the SPDM
# Header Fields" WAS everything a signature had to cover. Adding two fields to
# Table 80 made a sentence in a different chapter false. 1.4.1 replaces the
# enumeration with an exclusion — "* except the Signature and
# RequesterVerifyData fields" — which is correct by construction for a field
# that does not exist yet.
#
# Three identifiers, three databases, and only one hit
# ----------------------------------------------------
# This is the only one of the three 2026 advisories with a CVE, and it scores
# LOWER than the two without. On the retrieval date:
#
#   api.github.com/repos/DMTF/libspdm/security-advisories   the record, HTTP 200
#   github.com/advisories/GHSA-chjj-xvqx-c8w4               404
#   cveawg.mitre.org/api/cve/CVE-2026-61810                 404
#   services.nvd.nist.gov ... ?cveId=CVE-2026-61810         totalResults: 0
#
# So a reader handed "CVE-2026-61810" and told to look it up finds nothing in
# the two places they would look. Standing rule 7 exists for exactly this, and
# it is the reason W10 refused to write these identifiers down before they had
# been checked.
#
# ★ Reading the vector is worth more than reading the score: VC:N/VI:H/VA:N
# says the defect costs integrity only — nothing is disclosed and nothing stops
# working — and AV:A says the attacker has to be on the same bus. Those two
# together are why 6.0 and not more.
#
# Not vendored, for third_party/dmtf-2026-0002.pin's reason, word for word.
